A request takes its quantum's counts of virtual time whatever the units, rather than TIME_UNITS / units counts for each.
A thread with many units would wait as long for its turn as one with a single unit,
and a request would lie further ahead of its virtual time than its quantum at its share.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work test qemu-replay
Report: a request is due further ahead than its quantum
Witness: fuzz lend-lender-woken

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -389,7 +389,7 @@ uint32_t turn_vtime(const struct core *core, const struct place *p, uint32_t off
 /* The counts of virtual time a request of the place's quantum takes; the place has units. */
 static uint32_t request_length(const struct place *p)
 {
-    return COUNT_PARTS * place_quantum(p) / place_units(p);
+    return COUNT_PARTS * place_quantum(p);
 }
 
